{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00057",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 2.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Hello, please sit down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.01,
      "end_seconds": 7.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Thanks. Sorry, um, I'm a little early."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.48,
      "end_seconds": 10.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Have you been waiting long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.98,
      "end_seconds": 14.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Only about ten minutes, um, no trouble."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.25,
      "end_seconds": 17.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "So, what's been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.79,
      "end_seconds": 30.87,
      "duration_seconds": 12.08,
      "text": "I mean, I'm here because of dizziness when I stand up. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.74,
      "end_seconds": 33.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.05,
      "end_seconds": 41.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Uh, I've had it for about a week. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.38,
      "end_seconds": 54.16,
      "duration_seconds": 10.78,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps. Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.6,
      "end_seconds": 85.97,
      "duration_seconds": 31.37,
      "text": "It happens a couple of times a week. Standing up quickly definitely sets it off. It's mild, honestly. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. And, And dark urine, too. With dark urine, I get some relief from drinking more water. I've had muscle cramps too, for about four days. And a very dry mouth as well, since last night. With very dry mouth, I'd say mild. Drinking water helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.58,
      "end_seconds": 92.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Have you had dizziness when you stand up before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.31,
      "end_seconds": 98.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "A bit, about six months ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.17,
      "end_seconds": 103.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.86,
      "end_seconds": 115.43,
      "duration_seconds": 10.57,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.7,
      "end_seconds": 119.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Any chest pain, confusion or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.86,
      "end_seconds": 121.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.91,
      "end_seconds": 125.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Any blood in the stool or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.55,
      "end_seconds": 133.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "No, uh, no blood in the stool or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.5,
      "end_seconds": 136.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.7,
      "end_seconds": 138.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.87,
      "end_seconds": 142.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.12,
      "end_seconds": 144.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.05,
      "end_seconds": 148.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.82,
      "end_seconds": 152.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.38,
      "end_seconds": 154.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.7,
      "end_seconds": 159.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Yes, I had a hysterectomy, about twelve years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.54,
      "end_seconds": 163.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Okay, is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.92,
      "end_seconds": 166.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Hmm, it's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.75,
      "end_seconds": 169.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.39,
      "end_seconds": 173.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.66,
      "end_seconds": 175.43,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.36,
      "end_seconds": 178.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "I smoke about ten cigarettes a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.24,
      "end_seconds": 184.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.43,
      "end_seconds": 186.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.65,
      "end_seconds": 190.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.42,
      "end_seconds": 205.29,
      "duration_seconds": 12.87,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.08,
      "end_seconds": 211.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.92,
      "end_seconds": 225.65,
      "duration_seconds": 12.73,
      "text": "I take glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast. I did try to ignore it for a while. I take telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.48,
      "end_seconds": 229.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.35,
      "end_seconds": 230.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.32,
      "end_seconds": 250.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. So, any long-term health problems I should know about? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.35,
      "end_seconds": 272.55,
      "duration_seconds": 19.2,
      "text": "Well, I've got diabetes. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. I've had high blood pressure, yes. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.95,
      "end_seconds": 280.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.92,
      "text": "Okay, diabetes, that's already on your record. Good to know. Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.32,
      "end_seconds": 285.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 286.78,
      "end_seconds": 294.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse 106, temp 36.7 degrees. Blood pressure 97 over 58, SpO2 97 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.13,
      "end_seconds": 300.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.93,
      "end_seconds": 308.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.15,
      "end_seconds": 313.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.78,
      "end_seconds": 315.48,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.24,
      "end_seconds": 320.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.44,
      "end_seconds": 335.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Your mouth is quite dry and the skin is a little slow to spring back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.62,
      "end_seconds": 358.05,
      "duration_seconds": 16.43,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.71,
      "end_seconds": 364.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.37,
      "end_seconds": 393.01,
      "duration_seconds": 25.64,
      "text": "Putting it all together, my working impression is dehydration from a stomach bug. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. It could also be an electrolyte imbalance, so we'll keep that open. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had dizziness when you stand up for about a week, mild, and no confusion or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.01,
      "end_seconds": 396.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Um, yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.03,
      "end_seconds": 401.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.32,
      "end_seconds": 405.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Okay, so thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.0,
      "end_seconds": 420.81,
      "duration_seconds": 14.81,
      "text": "I'm going to order a kidney function test, for dehydration. Let's get blood salts, for dehydration. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'd like you to take ORS, 1 sachet, after each loose motion, for two days. That's for dehydration."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.27,
      "end_seconds": 422.11,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.58,
      "end_seconds": 449.19,
      "duration_seconds": 25.61,
      "text": "Small, frequent sips are better than a big glass at once, and keep going even if you don't feel thirsty. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. If you faint or can't keep any fluids down, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Come back next week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 450.56,
      "end_seconds": 455.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Yeah, um, sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 456.91,
      "end_seconds": 460.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 462.25,
      "end_seconds": 465.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "So, I come back next week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 466.44,
      "end_seconds": 471.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 471.75,
      "end_seconds": 475.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}